verses.text:
How{a} she sits alone,{b}
the city once thronged with people!
She has become like a widow,
she who was great among the nations;
a princess among the provinces
has been put to forced labor.

She sobs{c} all night long,
tears streaming down her face;
among all those who loved her
not one is left to console her;
all her companions have deceived her
and turned against her.

Judah{d} has been carried off, afflicted
and worked hard as a slave;
she lives among foreign peoples
and has found no place to rest;
all who chased her caught her
in the tight passes.

Zion’s highways{e} are in mourning,
with no pilgrims arriving for the festivals;
every gate of hers lies deserted;
her priests sigh;
her maidens are wretched,{f}
and as for her—bitterness.

Her foes{g} have become the head;
her enemies are at ease,
for Yahweh has afflicted her
for the multitude of her transgressions;
her little children have gone away,
captives before the foe.

Grievously{k} has Jerusalem sinned;
therefore she has become a thing unclean;{l}
all who honored her despise her,
for they have seen her nakedness;
she herself groans
and turns away.

Her uncleanness{m} is in her skirts;
she gave no thought to her end;
astonishingly she has come down,
with none to comfort her.
“See, O Yahweh, my affliction,
for the enemy has magnified himself!”

His hand{n} the adversary has thrust out
upon every treasure of hers;
for she watched the pagans
march into her holy place—
those you had forbidden
to join your congregation.{o}

“Is it{q} nothing to you, all you who pass along the road?{r}
Look and see
if there is any pain like my pain,
which was dealt out to me,
which Yahweh inflicted
on the day of his fierce anger.

Out of the heights{s} he hurled fire;
down into my bones he drove it;{t}
he stretched a net to snare my feet;
he made me turn back;
he left me forlorn,
sick the whole day through.

My offenses{u} are fastened as a yoke;{v}
his hand has woven them together;
they have been lifted onto my neck;
he has drained my strength;
the Lord has delivered me
into the power of those I cannot resist.

The Lord{w} has thrown aside
every warrior among my people;
he has called a gathering to wipe out
my young men;
the Lord has stomped the grapes
of Judah’s virgin daughter.

For these things{x} I weep;
my eye, my eye runs down with water;
for far from me is a comforter,
one to restore my life;
my children are desolate,
for the enemy has prevailed.”

Zion{y} reaches out with her hands;
no one is there to console her;
Yahweh issued orders concerning Jacob:
those around him must be his adversaries;
Jerusalem has turned into
something defiled in their midst.

“Yahweh{z} is in the right,
for I defied what he commanded;{aa}
listen, all you peoples,
and look at my suffering;
my girls and my young men
have been taken prisoner.

See,{ac} O Yahweh, for I am in distress;
my inner parts churn;
my heart is turned over within me,
for I have been very rebellious.
Outside the sword bereaves;
inside, it is like death.

They heard{ad} that I groan,
with none to comfort me;
all my enemies heard of my trouble;
they rejoice that you have done it.
Bring on the day you have proclaimed,
and let them be as I am.

May every{ae} wicked deed of theirs come into your view;
treat them harshly,
as harshly as you treated me
because of every rebellion of mine;
for many are my sighs,
and sick is my heart.”

Ah, how{a} the Lord in his wrath
has wrapped daughter Zion in cloud!{b}
Out of the sky to the dust he has hurled
Israel’s glory;
his own footrest{c} he has put out of mind
in the day of his fury.

Pitilessly{d} the Lord has gulped down
every homestead of Jacob;
in his rage he has demolished
daughter Judah’s fortresses;
he has leveled them to the earth;
kingdom and rulers he has desecrated.

In fierce anger he has chopped off{e}
all Israel’s strength;
he has pulled back his right hand
when the enemy came;
he has blazed up against Jacob like a fire in flames
consuming everything near.

He has drawn{f} his bow like an enemy,
his right hand poised like an adversary;
he has killed everything pleasing to see
in the tent of Daughter Zion;
like fire, his rage has poured out.

The Lord{g} has become like an enemy;
he has swallowed up Israel;
he has swallowed up all her palaces;
he has laid waste his strongholds,
and multiplied in daughter Judah
mourning and moaning.{h}

He has wrecked{i} his booth like a garden;
he has laid waste his meeting place;
Yahweh has made Zion forget
appointed feast and sabbath,
and in the indignation of his anger
has spurned king and priest.

His altar{j} the Lord has spurned,
his holy place renounced;
into the enemy’s grip he has handed over
the ramparts of her citadels;
in Yahweh’s house they made an uproar
like the din of a festival day.

Yahweh{k} resolved to wreck
daughter Zion’s wall;
he stretched the surveyor’s cord;
his hand he did not draw back from ruin;
he set bulwark and wall to grieving;
both alike waste away.

Sunk{l} into the ground are her gates;
he has ruined and broken her bars;
her king and her princes are among the nations;
there is no instruction;{m}
her prophets also find
no vision from Yahweh.

Silent on the earth{n} sit
daughter Zion’s elders;
dust they have tossed upon their heads;
sackcloth they have wrapped round;
Jerusalem’s maidens
droop their heads to the earth.

My eyes{o} are spent with tears;
my inner parts churn;
my liver{p} is poured out on the ground
because of the ruin of the daughter of my people,
as infant and nursing child faint
in the squares of the city.

All your enemies{w} have opened{v}
their mouths wide at you;
they whistle and grind their teeth;
they cry, “We have devoured her!
This is the day we waited for;
we have lived to see it!”

Yahweh{x} has carried out his plan;
he has accomplished the decree
he ordained long ago;
he has demolished without mercy;
he has let the enemy gloat over you
and raised your adversaries’ strength.

Their heart{y} cried out to the Lord.{z}
O wall of daughter Zion,
let tears run down like a torrent
day and night!
Give yourself no respite;
let not the pupil of your eye be still!

Arise,{aa} cry out in the night,
at the beginning of the watches!{ab}
Pour out your heart like water
before the face of the Lord!
Lift up your hands to him
for the lives of your little ones,
who faint for hunger
at the head of every street.{ac}

They lie{ae} on the ground in the streets,
young and old;
my young women and my young men
have fallen by the sword;
you have slain them in the day of your anger;
you have slaughtered without pity.

You summoned,{af} as to a day of appointed feast,
my terrors from all around;
and on the day of Yahweh’s anger
none escaped or survived;
those whom I cherished and reared
my enemy has destroyed.”

Even jackals{c} bare the breast
and suckle their young;
but the daughter of my people has turned cruel,
like the ostriches in the wilderness.{d}

Her princes{i} were brighter than snow,{j}
whiter than milk;
their bodies were ruddier than coral,
their form like lapis lazuli.

Blacker{k} than charcoal their faces have grown;
in the lanes no one knows them;
their hide clings shrunken to their frame,
withered like a stick.

Yahweh{n} has used up his rage;
he has unleashed his fierce anger;
he lit a fire in Zion
that has devoured her foundations.

“Off with you! Defiled!”{r} they shouted at them;
“Off, off! Keep your hands away!”
So they ran and roamed about;
among the peoples men said,
“Here they may lodge no more.”

Yahweh’s own presence{s} has dispersed them;{t}
no more will he look upon them;
for priests there was no respect,
for elders no kindness.

Still{u} our eyes failed,
looking in vain for help;
from our watchtower we watched
for a nation that could not save.{v}

Our footsteps{w} they stalked,
barring us from walking in our own plazas;
near was our finish, full our days;
yes, our finish had arrived.

Swifter{x} were our pursuers
than the eagles of the heavens;
on the mountains they chased us;
in the wilderness they lay in wait for us.

Be joyful{aa} and celebrate, daughter of Edom,
you who live in the land of Uz!{ab}
The cup will come around to you too;
you will get drunk and expose your nakedness.

Your guilt,{ac} daughter of Zion, has been paid in full;
he will not keep you in exile any longer;
but your guilt, daughter of Edom, he will punish;
he will lay bare your sins.
